{"id":"neemo-2025","slug":"neemo-2025","sub":null,"name":"Neemo Finance","date":"2025-07-05","one_liner":"A bot called the open drain function (0x03b79c24) that a key thief's proxy upgrade had added, one block (12 s) later, before the thief ever used it: 114.53 ETH of weETH for 0.02 ETH in fees. It returned 91.634 ETH (80%) to Neemo nine days later.","bot":"anon bot 0xb750 (executor 0x1a61249f)","race_type":"deploy-window-copy","narrative":["(1) Attacker: the proxy's owner/admin key (EOA 0x7e9b11d0aa215e0f1a7f62534c7c93fc340d493d, funded 2025-05-23 by 0x067cbde2, the address that created and upgraded the same proxy in Feb 2025; it made 3 upgradeToAndCall calls on the proxy that day) was used on 2025-07-05 to CREATE implementation 0xbc4b1d58b28c497b7afda6fb90fe1471fa0672cc (block 22855567 idx 107, 0x1040fe774fb487caa0102e876d13c5850e7181b6ee6cdf383a5cffd3d004e486) and call upgradeToAndCall on the proxy 0x54cd23460df45559fd5feeaada7ba25f89c13525 (block 22855568 idx 130, 0xcd4a637da42ef5db0b7b6a1592c99a594530852f91e806d8c12ce0b587579373). The new implementation equals the previous one plus exactly three new selectors (incidents/neemo-2025/impl_diff.json); 0x03b79c24(address to) has no msg.sender check and moves the proxy's entire weETH balance to `to`.","(2) Bot: EOA 0xb750e3165de458eae09904cc7fad099632860b0f (sender of ~700 routine txs to its executor 0x1a61249f6f4f9813c55aa3b02c69438607272ed3 since 2024-06-30) sent tx 0xa57ec56af91ec70517ca71ca50101958d9c2ec9fdb61edcf35a9081c375725c2 at block 22855569 position 0, 12 s (one block) after the upgrade block, 150 gwei priority fee against a 0.28 gwei base fee (next highest priority fee in the block 20 gwei). Its call tree enters the proxy with 0x03b79c24(<its own executor>), receives 106.929468 weETH, swaps it to 114.534060 WETH on the weETH/WETH Uniswap V3 pool and unwraps to the bot EOA.","(3) Call diff: the bot's victim-side call subtree (6 calls) is identical to the same function called by the key-holder EOA on a local anvil fork at block 22855568; only the recipient argument differs (38 hex chars) - incidents/neemo-2025/call_diff.json. The bot's exact calldata replayed on the fork reproduces the mainnet gas (137,752).","(4) Limits: the key holder never called 0x03b79c24 on-chain from any address (trace_filter of every call to the proxy over blocks 22855560-22862000, then the Etherscan tx list to 2026-10-21: only the upgrade, the bot, and three later calls). So there is no attacker drain tx, pending or reverted, to compare against. That the attacker meant to call it is inferred from the function being theirs and from the Neemo/Defimon account; the attacker's own post-upgrade calls were different selectors (0x53474b2c at block 22855612, 0x97e44edc at 22855836). Neither the upgrade tx nor the bot tx is in mempool-dumpster although 52-58%% of the txs in their blocks are; both are private flow (or missed)."],"chain":"ethereum","verdict":"confirmed-onchain","t0_ms":1751749415000,"pre_merge":false,"premerge_note":null,"slot":12077116,"block":{"number":22855569,"hash":"0x5308275cdb90ddec7f94b22ccf23a3c6ee9a1aea1ae81a1eea3bca0a32637d54","ts_ms":1751749415000,"ntx":159,"builder":"BuilderNet","fee_recipient":"0xdadb0d80178819f2319190d340ce9a924f783711","gas_used":13917060,"base_fee_gwei":0.279228836,"raw":{"block":"raw/rpc/block_22855569.json","receipts":"raw/rpc/receipts_22855569.json","trace":"raw/rpc/trace_block_22855569.json","slot":null}},"strip":[[0,1,"bot",150.0,0.0],[1,1,"",20.0,0.0],[2,1,"",7.493,0.0],[3,1,"",5.02,0.0],[4,1,"",5.0,0.0],[5,1,"",5.0,0.0],[6,1,"",5.0,0.0],[7,1,"",4.721,0.0],[8,1,"",4.721,0.0],[9,1,"",0.032,0.0],[10,1,"",7.141,0.0],[11,1,"",2.0,0.0],[12,1,"",2.0,0.0],[13,1,"",2.0,0.0],[14,1,"",2.0,0.0],[15,1,"",2.0,0.0],[16,1,"",2.0,0.0],[17,1,"",2.0,0.0],[18,1,"",7.387,0.0],[19,1,"",3.1,0.0],[20,1,"",3.0,0.0],[21,1,"",2.071,0.0],[22,1,"",2.061,0.0],[23,1,"",2.0,0.0],[24,1,"",2.0,0.0],[25,1,"",2.0,0.0],[26,1,"",2.0,0.0],[27,1,"",2.0,0.0],[28,1,"",2.0,0.0],[29,1,"",2.